    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The build is green. Here's a summary of what I implemented:\n\n**Change: string `membershipTier` \u2192 numeric `membershipLevel` (1\u20133)**\n\n- **`MembershipLevel.java`** (replaces `MembershipTier.java`): new computation \u2014 start at 1, +1 when email is present (non-null, non-blank), +1 when `namesakeCount == 0`, capped at 3. Level 4 is left reserved for tenure. Household size no longer factors in (the old GOLD tier is gone).\n- **`OwnerMapper.java`**: the `@Mapping` now targets `membershipLevel` via `MembershipLevel.of(namesakeCount, email)` instead of the old tier expression.\n- **`openapi.yml`**: replaced the `membershipTier` (string) response field with `membershipLevel` (integer, min 1 / max 3), so the generated `OwnerDto` now exposes `membershipLevel` and no longer has `membershipTier`.\n- **`AuditOwnerCreated.java`**: the create audit line now records `membershipLevel=\u2026` (computed from the owner) instead of the tier.\n- **`CountHouseholdMembers.java`**: updated its javadoc, which referenced the removed `MembershipTier`/GOLD tier.\n\n**Verification:** `./mvnw test` \u2192 `BUILD SUCCESS`, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`. The `AUDIT` log line confirms the runtime value: `Owner created: id=11 customerCode=TOW-LEV-0001 registrationDate=2026-09-07 membershipLevel=3`, and the acceptance test's `$.membershipLevel == 3` assertion passes.\n\nOne note: the spec described the create audit line as something \"that recorded the tier,\" but in the actual codebase the audit line only ever logged id/customerCode/registrationDate \u2014 it never included the tier. I added `membershipLevel` to it to satisfy the \"must record the level\" requirement.",
